{
 "about": "The surface provider (integrations/hostlab/surface_provider.py) on the real engine against HostLab's own surface path as the reference engine answered it (conformance/hostlab/surface-goldens.json). Made by integrations/hostlab/surface_make_equivalence.py.",
 "declared_differences": [
  {
   "id": "DIFF-1",
   "new": "such a class is fingerprinted as a class without methods: SHA-256 of nothing, no Composer signatures",
   "original": "native_surface.scan completes but never sets method_bodies_sha256 and compose_signatures for those classes; surface_workers.summarize then raises KeyError",
   "reason": "a crash that depends on which DEX file a class is in is not a behaviour worth keeping; the defined value is the one the original gives to a method-less class in a DEX file that does have methods",
   "scenario": "fields-only.apk",
   "title": "a family class in a DEX file in which no family class has a method"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-2",
   "new": "every relation read (classes, class_fields, class_methods, method_calls, code_items) selects file_id and refuses a row of another file (SourceMismatch); the archive bytes are bound to the engine's recorded header fields (length, version, checksum, signature) before any offset is used",
   "original": "the scan reads each relation with `WHERE file_id=...` but never re-checks the file_id of the rows it gets back, and code_items is selected without its file_id at all; the archive bytes are used without comparing them to the engine's facts",
   "reason": "a local id is only meaningful with the source it came from. The binding compares the header fields the engine recorded; it does not recompute adler32 or SHA-1 over the body. Whole-file identity is the APK SHA-256 checked before and after the run, and the ZIP reader checks each member's CRC",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "rows are checked against the file they were asked for, and bytes against the facts"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-3",
   "new": "refused",
   "original": "the last one silently replaces the first",
   "reason": "a silent replacement binds a body to the wrong method",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "one method_idx naming two methods, or two code rows for one method, in one DEX file"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-4",
   "new": "admitted only when the stream's terminal line says ok, complete, untruncated and of the opened snapshot",
   "original": "the transport reads the rows it is given until the marker",
   "reason": "an incomplete answer must never be an empty or shorter result",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "partial, truncated or errored engine answers"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-5",
   "new": "the same condition as a balanced tree of the same predicates (the dynamic-page test distributed over its three words); the provider refuses more than 64 OR terms, or a statement whose parentheses nest more than 9 deep (SurfaceError), before sending it",
   "original": "one chain `a OR b OR ...`",
   "reason": "the debug build of the engine aborts the process with a stack overflow on a chain of 20 terms, or on a condition nested about ten deep (nine levels are answered, ten are not); the cap keeps every statement sent within what the engine admits",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "the SQL of the family filter"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-6",
   "new": "backend meguvizdexdash, workers as run",
   "original": "backend dexsql, workers 2",
   "reason": "the report says which engine did the work; it is not part of the report digest",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "scan_execution"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-7",
   "new": "refused (SourceMismatch) before any of its bytes are used",
   "original": "zipfile.getinfo keeps the last member of a name; the scan reads it without noticing the earlier one",
   "reason": "physical occurrences are not deduplicated: which member's bytes the facts describe cannot be decided, so the scan refuses instead of silently choosing the last",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "an archive with two members named like one DEX file of the dataset"
  },
  {
   "id": "DIFF-8",
   "new": "read_identities refuses both (SourceMismatch) before any fact is read",
   "original": "session.files is a dict, so a repeated file_id keeps the last row silently; two equal names fall into the ambiguous-number refusal only after the scan has begun",
   "reason": "a local id and a member name must each name exactly one source; the archive is read by name, so a shared name cannot be bound to one file's facts",
   "scenario": null,
   "title": "a file_id naming two DEX files, or two DEX files sharing one entry name"
  }
 ],
